# The buried oxide is the thermal resistance to the substrate: a thicker one makes the shifter more efficient and slower.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Buried oxide 3 um thick
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=60 ymin=-10 ymax=6
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 6
rect si -0.25 0.25 3 3.25
rect tin -1 1 5 5.25
heater h xmin=-1 xmax=1 ymin=5 ymax=5.25 power=0.1
probe wg xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=3 ymax=3.25
expect response wg h 219.111002 1e-7
expect pi_power wg h 19.0162366 1e-7
expect peak 45.6782584 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 15360
